    "chunks": [
      {
        "chunk_id": "c-B-12",
        "source_id": "S-B",
        "paragraph": "para 12",
        "text": "We have considered the submissions. The view taken in Alpha v. Beta (2001) 1 SCC 100 is hereby overruled. Accordingly the appeal is allowed."
      },
      {
        "chunk_id": "c-B-15",
        "source_id": "S-B",
        "paragraph": "para 15",
        "text": "On the second point: With respect, we doubt the correctness of the view in Iota v. Kappa (1999) 4 SCC 88. The matter does not need to go further."
      },
      {
        "chunk_id": "c-B-20",
        "source_id": "S-B",
        "paragraph": "para 20",
        "text": "Here We overrule the decision in Alpha v. Beta (2001) 1 SCC 100 to that extent. That is the end of the matter."
      },
      {
        "chunk_id": "c-C-3",
        "source_id": "S-C",
        "paragraph": "para 3",
        "text": "The learned Judge observed: We follow the decision in Nu v. Xi (2010) 1 SCC 1 and hold accordingly. The reasoning is sound."
      },
      {
        "chunk_id": "c-C-4",
        "source_id": "S-C",
        "paragraph": "para 4",
        "text": "Next: The ratio of Iota v. Kappa (1999) 4 SCC 88 has since been doubted by two Benches of this Court. We keep that in mind."
      },
      {
        "chunk_id": "c-C-5",
        "source_id": "S-C",
        "paragraph": "para 5",
        "text": "It is argued otherwise but We follow the decision in Nu v. Xi (2010) 1 SCC 1 and hold accordingly. Nothing more is needed."
      },
      {
        "chunk_id": "c-C-9",
        "source_id": "S-C",
        "paragraph": "para 9",
        "text": "Looking at the record: We hold that the decision in Gamma v. Delta (1990) 2 SCC 50 was rendered per incuriam, as it ignored binding precedent. We say no more."
      },
      {
        "chunk_id": "c-D-7",
        "source_id": "S-D",
        "paragraph": "para 7",
        "text": "The respondent says so. It was submitted that the decision in Alpha v. Beta (2001) 1 SCC 100 ought to be overruled. We do not accept that."
      },
      {
        "chunk_id": "c-E-2",
        "source_id": "S-E",
        "paragraph": "para 2",
        "text": "Mr. Counsel is right in this: The decision in Alpha v. Beta (2001) 1 SCC 100 has not been overruled by any Bench of this Court. It stays on the books."
      },
      {
        "chunk_id": "c-C-6",
        "source_id": "S-C",
        "paragraph": "para 6",
        "text": "Distinguishing now: The decision in Lambda v. Mu (2005) 6 SCC 12 is clearly distinguished on facts, since there the lease had expired. The present lease is still running."
      }
    ],
